WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.956
His published paper asks how software can read

00:00:02.956 --> 00:00:05.749
inkless writing carved into damaged palm
leaves.

00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:08.865
It describes checking the leaf's surface and
using adaptive

00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:11.717
thresholding to separate faint grooves from
the grain.

00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:15.540
The paper explores transformer-based
transcription.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.020
The public prototype uses geometric features
and a Malayalam word list.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.169
A next step is to test a trained recognizer on

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:26.592
held-out manuscripts and measure character
errors.
